class Solution {
    public boolean isPrime(int n) {
        if (n < 2) {
            return false;
        }

        for (int divisor = 2; (long) divisor * divisor <= n; divisor++) {
            if (n % divisor == 0) {
                return false;
            }
        }

        return true;
    }
}
```

Time complexity: `O(sqrt(n))`.
Space complexity: `O(1)`.

This keeps the prime test close to the definition: a prime number has no divisor other than 1 and itself. The loop starts at 2 and stops at the square root, which is enough to find a factor if one exists.

Numbers 0 and 1 are handled before the loop because neither is prime. Negative values are also rejected by the same condition.

